{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01069",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.63,
      "end_seconds": 2.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Right, morning, come on through."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 3.44,
      "end_seconds": 8.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.78,
      "end_seconds": 14.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 16.28,
      "end_seconds": 23.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "It's sore red lumps, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.01,
      "end_seconds": 27.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 28.01,
      "end_seconds": 51.36,
      "duration_seconds": 23.35,
      "text": "She is on escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day, I give it to her. Actually, she is on iron tablets, once a day for my blood count, I give it to her. She takes metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day for the heart rhythm. She takes face wash, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.15,
      "end_seconds": 58.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Alright, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.63,
      "end_seconds": 65.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Around nearly five years... no wait, it's more like two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.81,
      "end_seconds": 73.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 73.79,
      "end_seconds": 78.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.87,
      "end_seconds": 96.61,
      "duration_seconds": 12.74,
      "text": "Actually, I was getting to that! There's spots on my face as well. Okay, so I've been feeling low about my skin too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.81,
      "end_seconds": 101.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.77,
      "end_seconds": 109.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.41,
      "end_seconds": 115.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.77,
      "end_seconds": 120.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 121.35,
      "end_seconds": 124.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Yes, that's right, that's how it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.43,
      "end_seconds": 130.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Have you had any joint pain or excess hair growth?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.25,
      "end_seconds": 146.56,
      "duration_seconds": 14.31,
      "text": "Well, no, no joint pain, no excess hair growth. I did have marks left after the spots at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.29,
      "end_seconds": 150.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Any fever, being pregnant or headaches?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.16,
      "end_seconds": 153.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.98,
      "end_seconds": 157.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.04,
      "end_seconds": 164.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.76,
      "end_seconds": 171.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.01,
      "end_seconds": 187.91,
      "duration_seconds": 11.9,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.3,
      "end_seconds": 193.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Okay, any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.01,
      "end_seconds": 202.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.65,
      "text": "I've got anxiety. Yes, low haemoglobin. I have an irregular heartbeat. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.4,
      "end_seconds": 206.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Right, and anything else to add?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.87,
      "end_seconds": 213.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Okay, I can see anxiety and an irregular heartbeat in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.62,
      "end_seconds": 232.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.84,
      "end_seconds": 237.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.06,
      "end_seconds": 240.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.03,
      "end_seconds": 245.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.87,
      "end_seconds": 250.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.96,
      "end_seconds": 253.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.01,
      "end_seconds": 259.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.17,
      "end_seconds": 273.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Right, that's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.4,
      "end_seconds": 296.21,
      "duration_seconds": 9.81,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 16, BP is 114 over 78, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, temp 37.0 degrees, pulse 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.85,
      "end_seconds": 333.72,
      "duration_seconds": 25.87,
      "text": "From what you've told me, I think we're dealing with moderate inflammatory acne at this stage. It could also be rosacea, so we'll keep that open. It could also be a hormonal cause, so we'll keep that open. Just to be sure I understood. You've had sore red lumps for two years, and no joint pain or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.58,
      "end_seconds": 337.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Um, yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.62,
      "end_seconds": 373.25,
      "duration_seconds": 33.63,
      "text": "Let's get blood tests, for acne treatment baseline. I'm going to put you on adapalene gel, 0.1 percent, once a night, for twelve weeks. It's for acne. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Use sunscreen daily, and the gel can sting for the first couple of weeks. I'd like you to see the dermatology clinic as well, and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.61,
      "end_seconds": 375.31,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.17,
      "end_seconds": 384.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.78,
      "end_seconds": 388.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Alright, uh, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.64,
      "end_seconds": 392.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Come back in twelve weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.57,
      "end_seconds": 397.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Okay, uh, I'll arrange it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.9,
      "end_seconds": 404.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "How would you describe the plan, so we're on the same page?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.94,
      "end_seconds": 416.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.78,
      "text": "So, I take the adapalene gel, 0.1 percent, once a night and come back in twelve weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 418.64,
      "end_seconds": 423.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "Alright, yes, exactly right. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.25,
      "end_seconds": 428.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "No, um, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}